```grf:context id="security-reporting"
{
  "format": "grf.public-document/v1",
  "title": "SECURITY",
  "content": "Security\n\nDo not send private keys, certificates, license identifiers, sensitive commands,\nserver source or private policies in public issues. Contact the verified release\nmaintainer privately through the hosting platform before sharing a vulnerability.\nNo dedicated security mailbox is published in this release candidate.\n\nAssess the public client as untrusted and inspect its commands before running.\nThe service must enforce authorization itself; a modified client must never be\nable to elevate a license, select another customer's policy, or retrieve internal\nrules. Customer-controlled local checks are not trusted evidence for the service.\n\nNever use an administrative SSH credential for customer enrollment. Never expose\ndebuggers, evaluator files, or administration routes through the public API.\n\nPlease report reproduction steps using synthetic data and the client version.\nDo not attempt denial of service or retrieve another customer's data."
}
```
